@@ -63,6 +63,33 @@ fwctl --device sensor-0042 update sensor-node-1.2.0.fwpkg
 fwctl --device sensor-0042 status
 ```
 
+## Staged updates
+
+A single `update` transfers, activates, health-checks, and confirms in one
+session. When the transfer window and the reboot window are hours apart, split
+the work:
+
+```sh
+# Minutes over serial, while the device keeps running confirmed firmware.
+fwctl --device sensor-0042 stage sensor-node-1.2.0.fwpkg
+
+# Later, from the staging journal alone: candidate, reboot, health check, confirm.
+fwctl staged
+fwctl --device sensor-0042 activate
+```
+
+`stage` stops after the device verifies the received image digest. It never
+selects the candidate slot and never reboots, so a device that is not activated
+keeps running its confirmed firmware. Each staged transfer is recorded in the
+staging journal, one record per device, newest replacing older.
+
+`activate` needs nothing but the device and that record. It reconnects, checks
+that the device still reports the same product, running firmware, rollback
+counter, and held transfer, re-checks the image digest, and only then moves boot
+state. If the device moved on, activation stops with `staged_update_lost` before
+touching boot state, and the stale record is dropped. Activating a device with
+no record reports `nothing_staged`.
+
 After an update, run `fwctl --device sensor-0042 history` to review the outcome
 recorded locally, or `fwctl doctor` if a device does not show up in `fwctl
 devices`.
